; worldsaves.eval - the saves a list shows follow the world in hand (code-review
; C207). Judged by tools/WorldTest.py phase 22, which runs it with -project on
; its scratch world.
;
; A `-project` run used to fix its save filter to the LAUNCH world for the whole
; process, so after a switch every list - Load, Continue, `load`, the editor's
; save sweeps - showed the first world's saves and none of the world in hand's.
; So: a save in the launch world (A), a switch to a new world, a save there (B)
; with a blob placed live (a spawn row naming its type), then
;   - `load` and `title status` must list B and not A (the -project rule still
;     holds, for the world the run is now in);
;   - the blob type, which nothing else in the new world names, is deleted, and
;     the delete must WARN that B still names it - the editor's sweep has to
;     find a save of the world in hand.
; WorldTest makes nothing of A here; phase 22 uses both saves after this run.
; It renames the saves AND the new world to this worktree's (wt_saves_<tag>):
; the lists pick saves by the world they name, in a folder every session shares.
logecho on
reset
save worldsaves_a
worlds new wt_saves
worlds load wt_saves
state
freeze on
spawn blob 7 7
save worldsaves_b
echo --- saves: listed after the switch ---
load
title status
echo --- saves: a type only a save names ---
reset
typerefs monsters blob
typeset delete monsters blob
